       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum for adults in a hospital setting, which is 3,200 mg/day. A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, even when kidney and liver function are normal.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), for mild to moderate pain\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or **800 mg four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum), for inflammatory conditions\n\n1600 mg may have been meant as the total daily dose. Tell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want the original dose, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note documenting that."
      }
